            "subject": "LU-12669 lov: slow and dead OST detection for degraded reads"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-02 11:50:38.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-15 07:42:17.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-12669 lov: peer-relative deadline for EC raid set reads",
        "message": "LU-12669 lov: peer-relative deadline for EC raid set reads\n\nA soft deadline based on an OST's own latency estimate catches an\nOST that suddenly stalls, but an OST that is persistently slower\nthan its peers moves its own estimate up and is never routed\naround, although a read of a whole raid set waits for it each time.\n\nFor a synchronous parallel direct read of an EC file, track each\nraid set it reads.  Once all but as many of its data stripes as the\nparity can stand in for have been read, give the reads of the other\nstripes a soft deadline of osc.*.slow_read_pct percent of the time\nthat took, at least osc.*.slow_read_min_ms of their own OSC, so a\nstraggler is abandoned and reconstructed from parity.  An RPC that\ncarries several stripes' pages is tracked for each of them, and\nptlrpcd rearms its timer when a soft deadline is brought forward\n(ptlrpc_request::rq_soft_reset).\n\nWhen reconstructing, use the survivor pages that readahead already\nread but no reader used yet (cl_page::cp_defer_uptodate) instead of\nreading them again, and submit the surviving data stripe reads of a\nrecovery group together instead of waiting for each in turn, with\ncl_io_submit_sync() split into cl_io_submit_start() and\ncl_io_submit_finish().\n\nAdd OBD_FAIL_OST_BRW_PAUSE_READ_IDX to delay the reads of chosen\nOSTs, and sanity-ec 77l-77n.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I6e4e76421e48ae1a8bc9b5fe647cab27c03ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
